Translation patch: `value::convert::{bigint, decimal, bigdecimal}`: num-bigint, rust_decimal and bigdecimal calls go through `trusted`

Change: `x.into()` (`From<i64>`/`From<u64>`), `parse_bytes(bytes, 10)`, `BigUint::from_i64`, `to_i64`/`to_u64`, `to_string().into()`, `Decimal::from_str`, `from_utf8`, and `x.try_into()` (`TryFrom<f32/f64> for BigDecimal`) become `trusted::*` helpers; `Ok`/`Err` matches on them become `Some`/`None` matches.
Why: these crates are not translated (see patch 40).
Behaviour: Identical: each helper is the call it replaces (`.ok()` where only `Ok`/`Err` was observed); `From<String> for Vec<u8>` is `into_bytes`.

